  "language_probability": 1,
  "text": "Put your hands under this automatic faucet and water starts without a touch. A small infrared sensor near the spout detects that your hands are there. An infrared LED sends out pulses of light that people cannot see. With no hands nearby, that light travels away and little returns to the receiver. Your hands reflect some of the infrared light back toward the sensor. When the return signal is strong enough, a controller opens a solenoid valve. Remove your hands, the reflection disappears and the valve closes again. So the faucet turns reflected infrared light into water flow without touch.",
